<title>BELGIUM: Belgacom sees further results growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>Belgacom sees further results growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian state telephone company Belgacom said on Thursday it expected to see further growth in its results, excluding extraordinary items, in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The Belgacom group will continue efforts to improve its competitive position in view of total deregulation of the telecoms market on January 1, 1998,&quot; it added in a statement.</p>
<p>In 1996 group net profit rose 21 percent to 13 billion francs, it said.  </p>
<p>Belgacom SA is 49 percent owned by a consortium comprising Ameritech, Singapore Telecom, TeleDanmark and three Belgian investors.</p>
<p>The remaining shares are held by the Belgian state.</p>
